#!/usr/bin/env python3
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# nyxus-voiced   ·   rev 2026-07-14 r1 (Cosmic Voice Control)
#
# Offline, wake-word voice assistant for the NYXUS Hyprland desktop.
# Say "Nyxus, <command>" to drive the desktop with your voice.
#
#   "Nyxus, lock down"                 -> loginctl lock-session
#   "Nyxus, launch terminal"           -> app launch (config app map)
#   "Nyxus, workspace three"           -> hyprctl dispatch workspace 3
#   "Nyxus, take a screenshot"         -> nyxus_screenshot.py
#   "Nyxus, toggle living wallpaper"   -> nyxus-live-wallpaper toggle
#   "Nyxus, mute" / "volume up"        -> wpctl set-{mute,volume}
#   "Nyxus, say hi"                    -> companion wave + alien chirp
#   "Nyxus, go to sleep"               -> daemon self-mutes (push-to-talk)
#
# DESIGN — offline-first, lightweight, NEVER crashes the session:
#   * STT backend is Vosk (python-vosk + a small model). Vosk is the
#     lightest always-on option: streaming, tiny (~50MB small EN model),
#     fully local, no network, ideal for continuous wake-word capture.
#   * If Vosk (or its model) is missing, the daemon logs a clear
#     "no STT backend" message and idles harmlessly — the parser and
#     dispatcher are fully exercised via --selftest / --simulate so the
#     whole pipeline is testable with no microphone at all.
#   * Mic capture prefers python-sounddevice; falls back to `pw-record`
#     (PipeWire) as a raw-PCM subprocess. Either feeds 16kHz mono s16le
#     into Vosk.
#   * Audio feedback reuses the alien sound theme via `nyxus-sound`.
#     Optional spoken TTS via espeak-ng or piper if present (never a
#     hard dependency — checked with shutil.which).
#
# PRIVACY: 100% local. No audio ever leaves the machine; there is no
# network code path. The mic is only opened while the daemon runs and
# is NOT muted (see `nyxus-voice mute` / push-to-talk toggle).
#
# CONFIG:  ~/.config/nyxus/voice.conf   (auto-created with defaults)
# LOG:     ~/.cache/nyxus/voice.log
# PID:     $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nyxus-voiced.pid
# MUTE:    $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nyxus-voiced.mute   (push-to-talk flag)
#
# USAGE (normally driven by the `nyxus-voice` CLI, not run directly):
#   nyxus-voiced                       run the daemon (foreground)
#   nyxus-voiced --selftest            run dispatcher unit tests, exit 0/1
#   nyxus-voiced --simulate "TEXT"     parse+dispatch one transcript (dry-run)
#   nyxus-voiced --simulate "TEXT" --execute   ...and actually run it
#   nyxus-voiced --print-config        show resolved config + backend status
#   nyxus-voiced --list-devices        list input devices (calibration)
#
